27T09:33:04Z","body":"Is there a reason we wouldn't want it working with inherited nodes with scripts? The workflow in my video of making a scene, attaching a script then loading that into another scene is very common in Godot and being able to quickly extend would be very handy.\n\nThe current functionality is a little confusing IMO.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563507584/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563510557","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100074#issuecomment-2563510557","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100074","id":2563510557,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YzBEd","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-27T09:36:49Z","updated_at":"2024-12-27T09:36:49Z","body":"Well, if you have custom type, it's more expected that you create instance by making a node of that type, not attaching a script to a node of a different type.\nMaking instance of a scene instantiates it as-is, so the script metadata is unchanged. If you created a node, but want to change it to custom type, just use Change Type, like you'd do with regular type.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563510557/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564074169","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100074#issuecomment-2564074169","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100074","id":2564074169,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y1Kq5","user":{"login":"afterlightgames","id":86094024,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2MDk0MDI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86094024?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterlightgames","html_url":"https://github.com/afterlightgames","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterlightgames/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterlightgames/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterlightgames/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterlightgames/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterlightgames/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterlightgames/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterlightgames/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterlightgames/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterlightgames/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-27T22:43:09Z","updated_at":"2024-12-27T22:52:22Z","body":"I think to ease this kind of confusion the extend script button ought to be shown if a script is present no matter what. It's not very clear why attaching a custom class script to an existing node wouldn't show the extend script button as long as the node is the correct type since it would effectively behave exactly the same way as if you added it the 'expected' way. Is there anything to gain from not showing it?\n\nIn any case, I think extending scripts is a common enough workflow to justify permanently adding it to the dock. There's no need to have complicated logic to determine whether or not a user 'needs' to see it.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564074169/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564083799","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100074#issuecomment-2564083799","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100074","id":2564083799,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y1NBX","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-27T23:12:19Z","updated_at":"2024-12-27T23:12:19Z","body":"Whether the dock shows Extend or Detach script is determined by custom script metadata, which stores the script the node was originally created with, whwich serves the same purpose as the node's actual type. Overwriting this metadata when attaching a script would be like changing the node type by attaching a different script. Like, imagine attaching CharacterBody2D script to Node2D would change the node type to CharacterBody2D. That's not a correct behavior.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564083799/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564159565","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100074#issuecomment-2564159565","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100074","id":2564159565,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y1fhN","user":{"login":"scotmcp","id":79280460,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MjgwNDYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79280460?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotmcp","html_url":"https://github.com/scotmcp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotmcp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotmcp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotmcp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotmcp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotmcp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotmcp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotmcp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotmcp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotmcp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-28T03:48:55Z","updated_at":"2024-12-28T03:51:40Z","body":"Well I can confirm the button does not appear in the toolbar despite it being present in the context menu. It is also my opinion that it should appear in the toolbar if there is something to extent.\n\nGodot v4.4.dev7 - Linux Mint 22 (Wilma) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 4 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Ti (nvidia; 550.120) - AMD Ryzen 7 5700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/74c69560-9d30-49a6-985d-acc093911c9e)\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564159565/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]